# The parts that cross a document, which is the `callActivity` population and not the whole part
# table. One row per part whose target lives in another filing.
#
# The pin is in the file name
#   Because it is not in the key, and a relation that restricts a dimension must declare it.
#   `|callActivity| + |subProcess| = |part|` is one law over two elements, and a law of that shape
#   lets a local part be rendered as a flow node. A local fusion is a partition of the composed
#   layer, not an activity inside it, so the two halves are two laws.
#
# Splitting them measures `invents`
#   Only a foreign part goes through `calledElement`, which is a QName of a process, and that is
#   the flattening that can put a cycle in the emitted call graph which `F` does not have. A law
#   over the union of both cannot say how much of the emission is exposed to it. This one can: it
#   is the exposed population.
-- diagrams/calls.sqlc pinned to the parts that leave their own document.
SELECT c.composition, c.composed_layer, c.part_notation, c.part_filing, c.part_layer
FROM (
    :compose(diagrams/calls.sqlc)
) c
WHERE NOT c.is_local
